From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab refactor <kebab@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:44:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OPTIONAL usb: typec: qcom: widen the vSafe5V poll tolerance

NOT IN THE DEFAULT SERIES. Add it back only if "vbus vsafe5v fail"
appears on every source attach again.

The supported way to express a slow VBUS rail is to tell the regulator
core about it, which the board does with
regulator-enable-ramp-delay = <1200000> on the MP2762A boost, backed
by the driver's own enable_time. regulator_enable() then returns only
once the rail is really up and the 250 ms poll below succeeds on the
first attach.

Keep this as a fallback: it teaches a generic Qualcomm Type-C driver
that all VBUS supplies might be slow, which is the wrong layer, but it
does not depend on the regulator honouring its ramp delay.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c
index bf985efe1..02d332f9d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c
@@ -310,11 +310,18 @@ static int qcom_pmic_typec_port_vbus_toggle(struct pmic_typec_port *pmic_typec_p
 		val = TYPEC_SM_VBUS_VSAFE0V;
 	}
 
-	/* Poll waiting for transition to required vSafe5V or vSafe0V */
+	/*
+	 * Poll waiting for transition to required vSafe5V or vSafe0V.
+	 *
+	 * 250 ms is the Type-C tSrcTurnOn budget, but a boost converter on a
+	 * multi-cell pack can take far longer: measured between 550 ms and
+	 * ~1.1 s on this board. The poll exits the moment the bit is set, so
+	 * a longer tolerance costs nothing when VBUS is quick.
+	 */
 	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(pmic_typec_port->regmap,
 				       pmic_typec_port->base + TYPEC_SM_STATUS_REG,
 				       sm_stat, sm_stat & val,
-				       100, 250000);
+				       100, 1200000);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_warn(pmic_typec_port->dev, "vbus vsafe%dv fail\n", on ? 5 : 0);
 
